  "title": "INS Nipun Commissioned for Deep-Sea and Submarine Rescue",
  "summary": "The Indian Navy has commissioned INS Nipun, a deep-sea diving vessel designed to support underwater operations, including saturation, air and heliox diving, and to provide rapid submarine rescue. This is the second such vessel commissioned into the Indian Navy, and it was built by Hindustan Shipyard Ltd.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The INS Nipun is a 119.4-meter long deep-sea diving vessel with a capacity of 10,500 tonnes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "INS Nipun has the capability to support diving operations up to 300 meters and provide rapid submarine rescue.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "INS Nipun was commissioned in Mumbai by Navy chief Admiral Krishna Swaminathan.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
